IMPORT prelude

-- Parliamentary Pensions Act 1978 (Singapore) -- who may be granted a pension for service as a Member of Parliament or as an
-- office-holder, and how much (ss 2, 2A, 3, 4, 5(1), (2)); when the pension is not payable (ss 3(4), (6), 4(4)); the option between
-- a full pension, a reduced pension with a gratuity, and a commuted pension gratuity, and the default when no option is made (s 7(1)
-- to (5)); assignment and attachment (s 12); reduction or withholding on a corruption conviction (s 13); and bankruptcy (s 15).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PPA1978.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The latest
-- amending Act annotated in the text and the Legislative History is Act 21 of 2012, the Parliamentary Pensions (Abolition) Act 2012,
-- whose section 5 amendments are listed as commencing on 21 May 2011 (a date earlier than the Bill's first reading, 13 August 2012).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0196 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to eligibility, amount, payability, the commutation option and the protective and forfeiture provisions. Not
-- encoded: the s 5(3), (4) suspension and lump-sum catch-up for office-holders pensioned before 21 May 2011; s 7(6) to (9) (reduction
-- on re-computation, the law in force at eligibility, transitional persons); s 8 (payment intervals); s 14 (President's restoration
-- for wife and children); s 15(3), (4) (President's application of a bankrupt's pension); ss 16, 17 (Pension Fund; regulations,
-- including the provident-fund opt-out in s 17(2), (3)); s 18 (persons under the repealed 1970 Act); and the counting of reckonable
-- service by dates -- the caller supplies the months that count.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Parliamentary Pensions Act 1978 -- pensions`

§§ `2 and 2A -- reckonable service and future Members`

-- s 2(1): "reckonable service" means service as a Member, or in an office, "on and after 3 June 1959 but not after 20 May 2011".
-- A "future Member" is, in short, a person who first becomes a Member after 1 January 1995 (and certain others who return or change
-- seat type after that date).
-- s 2A(1): "a future Member is not eligible for any pension or gratuity ... in respect of his or her reckonable service as a future
-- Member". (2)(a): a future Member who holds office "remains eligible for a pension ... in respect of his or her reckonable service in
-- that office"; (b): a person who already had the minimum service for a s 3 pension on the day before becoming a future Member
-- remains eligible in respect of service "as of that date".
-- (3): a nominated Member on 1 January 1995 is not eligible in respect of service as a Member on or after that date.
--
-- The months that count toward a Member's pension: reckonable months (before 21 May 2011) less those served as a future Member.
GIVEN `reckonable months as a Member` IS A NUMBER, `of which months as a future Member` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months that count for a Member's pension` MEANS
    `reckonable months as a Member` MINUS `of which months as a future Member`

-- Office service is NOT cut down for a future Member (s 2A(2)(a)), only by the 20 May 2011 end of reckonable service.

§§ `3 -- pension for service as a Member`

-- s 3(1): a person who ceases to be a Member "may be granted a pension under this section if he or she has not less than 9 years'
-- reckonable service as a Member (whether continuously or not)".
GIVEN `has ceased to be a Member` IS A BOOLEAN, `months that count` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Member's pension may be granted` IF
    `has ceased to be a Member` AND `months that count` AT LEAST 108

-- s 3(2): "(a) in respect of every completed year of reckonable service -- at the rate of one-thirtieth (1/30) of his or her annual
-- salary; and (b) in respect of any remaining uncompleted year ... one-three-hundred and sixtieth (1/360) part of his or her annual
-- salary for each completed month". (3): "must not exceed two-thirds of his or her annual salary". (5): "annual salary" is the annual
-- equivalent of the highest monthly rate of salary (excluding non-pensionable allowances) during reckonable service as a Member.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN `completed months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`completed years in` `completed months` MEANS FLOOR (`completed months` DIVIDED BY 12)

GIVEN `months of service` IS A NUMBER, `annual salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Member's annual pension` MEANS
    `the smaller of`
        (    (`completed years in` `months of service`) TIMES `annual salary` DIVIDED BY 30
        PLUS (`months of service` MINUS 12 TIMES (`completed years in` `months of service`)) TIMES `annual salary` DIVIDED BY 360)
        (`annual salary` TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 3)

§§ `4 and 5 -- pension for service in an office`

-- "office" means Prime Minister, Deputy Prime Minister, Speaker, Senior Minister, Minister, Senior Minister of State, Minister of
-- State, Mayor, Senior Parliamentary Secretary, Parliamentary Secretary or Political Secretary (s 2(1)).
-- s 4(1): a pension "in addition to any pension that may be granted ... under section 3" if the person "ceases at any time to hold
-- office and has not less than 8 years' reckonable service as an office-holding Member".
-- s 5(1): an office-holding Member with 8 years, who has "attained 55 years of age" and has not previously been granted a s 4 pension
-- may be granted one "despite the fact that he or she has not ceased to hold office"; (2): but not one "who attains 55 years of age on
-- or after 21 May 2011".
GIVEN `has ceased to hold office` IS A BOOLEAN, `months as an office-holding Member` IS A NUMBER,
      `attained 55 before 21 May 2011` IS A BOOLEAN, `already granted a section 4 pension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an office pension may be granted` IF
        `months as an office-holding Member` AT LEAST 96
    AND (    `has ceased to hold office`
         OR  (`attained 55 before 21 May 2011` AND (NOT `already granted a section 4 pension`)))

-- s 4(2): per office, "(a) ... every completed year ... one-twenty-seventh (1/27) of his or her annual salary in that office; and
-- (b) ... one-three-hundred and twenty-fourth (1/324) part ... for each completed month". (3): the total "must not exceed two-thirds
-- of the highest annual salary of any office held by him or her".
GIVEN `months in the office` IS A NUMBER, `annual salary in the office` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the uncapped pension for one office` MEANS
         (`completed years in` `months in the office`) TIMES `annual salary in the office` DIVIDED BY 27
    PLUS (`months in the office` MINUS 12 TIMES (`completed years in` `months in the office`)) TIMES `annual salary in the office` DIVIDED BY 324

GIVEN `months in the first office` IS A NUMBER, `salary in the first office` IS A NUMBER,
      `months in the second office` IS A NUMBER, `salary in the second office` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the office pension over two offices` MEANS
    `the smaller of`
        (`the uncapped pension for one office` `months in the first office` `salary in the first office`
         PLUS `the uncapped pension for one office` `months in the second office` `salary in the second office`)
        ((IF `salary in the first office` AT LEAST `salary in the second office` THEN `salary in the first office` ELSE `salary in the second office`)
         TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 3)

§§ `3(4), (6), 4(4), 13 and 15 -- when a granted pension is paid`

-- s 3(4): a Member's pension "is not payable in respect of any period during which he or she is again a Member or is a candidate for
-- election to Parliament". (6): a person who ceases to be a Member on dissolution "is to be treated as a candidate for election from
-- the date of the dissolution if he or she seeks re-election at the next general election".
-- s 4(4): an office pension "is not payable in respect of any period during which he or she is again an office-holding Member" --
-- nothing about candidacy.
-- s 15(2): if a pensioner "is adjudged a bankrupt ... such pension forthwith ceases"; (5): restored "with effect from the date of the
-- discharge" on "a full and proper discharge".
-- s 13(2): the President may "reduce or altogether ... withhold" a pension (dealt with below; here a flag that it was withheld).
GIVEN `is again a Member` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a candidate for election` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `left on dissolution and seeks re-election at the next general election` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN, `withheld by the President` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Member's pension is payable for the period` IF
        (NOT `is again a Member`)
    AND (NOT `is a candidate for election`)
    AND (NOT `left on dissolution and seeks re-election at the next general election`)
    AND (NOT `is an undischarged bankrupt`)
    AND (NOT `withheld by the President`)

GIVEN `is again an office-holding Member` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a candidate for election` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN, `withheld by the President` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the office pension is payable for the period` IF
        (NOT `is again an office-holding Member`)
    AND (NOT `is an undischarged bankrupt`)
    AND (NOT `withheld by the President`)

-- s 15(1): no pension or gratuity "may be so granted if, at the date he or she became eligible ... the person has been adjudged a
-- bankrupt or declared insolvent by judgment of a court of competent jurisdiction in Singapore or elsewhere and has not obtained his or
-- her discharge".
GIVEN `bankrupt or insolvent at the date of eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN, `discharged by then` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bankruptcy bars the grant` IF
    `bankrupt or insolvent at the date of eligibility` AND (NOT `discharged by then`)

§§ `7 -- the option: full pension, reduced pension and gratuity, or commuted gratuity`

-- s 7(1): (a) a future Member who becomes an office-holding Member -- "(i) a full pension under section 4 without any gratuity; or
-- (ii) a commuted pension gratuity without any pension"; (b) a future Member who keeps eligibility under s 2A(2)(b), or a Member
-- (including an office-holding Member) who is not a future Member -- (i) a full pension, "(ii) a reduced pension at the rate of
-- two-thirds of the full pension together with a gratuity equal to twelve and one-half (12 1/2) times the annual value of one-third of
-- the full pension; or (iii) a commuted pension gratuity"; (c) a person granted a s 4 pension who becomes an office-holding Member
-- again -- (i) full pension or (ii) commuted gratuity, for the further service.
DECLARE Pensioner IS ONE OF
    `a future Member who became an office-holder`
    `a Member who is not a future Member`
    `a future Member who kept eligibility under section 2A(2)(b)`
    `a pensioned office-holder who returned to office`

DECLARE Option IS ONE OF
    `a full pension without any gratuity`
    `a reduced pension with a gratuity`
    `a commuted pension gratuity without any pension`

GIVEN `the pensioner` IS A Pensioner, `the option` IS AN Option
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the option is open to` IF
    CONSIDER `the option`
    WHEN `a reduced pension with a gratuity` THEN
        CONSIDER `the pensioner`
        WHEN `a Member who is not a future Member` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a future Member who kept eligibility under section 2A(2)(b)` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `full pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduced pension` MEANS `full pension` TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 3

GIVEN `full pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the gratuity with a reduced pension` MEANS 12.5 TIMES (`full pension` DIVIDED BY 3)

-- s 7(5): the commuted pension gratuity is "a capital sum ascertained by multiplying the prescribed commutation factor by the amount of
-- pension that the person concerned is eligible for". The factor is prescribed by the President (s 2(1)) and is not in the Act.
GIVEN `commutation factor` IS A NUMBER, `full pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the commuted pension gratuity` MEANS `commutation factor` TIMES `full pension`

-- s 7(2)(b): the option is exercisable "not later than 30 days after the date when the person becomes eligible", except that the
-- President may, "if it appears in the circumstances equitable", allow it later, before payment. (3): a person who "fails to exercise
-- the option ... is deemed to have opted to receive a commuted pension gratuity without any pension". (4): once exercised it "must not
-- be revoked".
GIVEN `made a choice` IS A BOOLEAN, `the choice` IS AN Option, `days after eligibility` IS A NUMBER,
      `President allowed a late option` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Option
`the option that applies` MEANS
    IF `made a choice` AND (`days after eligibility` AT MOST 30 OR `President allowed a late option`)
    THEN `the choice`
    ELSE `a commuted pension gratuity without any pension`

§§ `12 -- not assignable, not attachable`

-- s 12: a pension or gratuity "is not assignable or transferable, except for the purpose of satisfying (a) a debt due to the
-- Government; or (b) an order of any court for the payment of periodical sums of money towards the maintenance of the wife or former
-- wife or minor child, whether legitimate or not", and "shall not be liable to be attached, sequestered or levied upon for or in respect
-- of any debt or claim whatever except a debt due to the Government".
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `a debt due to the Government`
    `a court maintenance order for a wife or former wife`
    `a court maintenance order for a minor child`
    `a court maintenance order for a husband or former husband`
    `a judgment debt owed to a private creditor`
    `a bank loan`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pension may be assigned to satisfy` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a debt due to the Government` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a court maintenance order for a wife or former wife` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a court maintenance order for a minor child` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pension may be attached for` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a debt due to the Government` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `13 -- corruption`

-- s 13(1): "No person has an absolute right to compensation for past services or to any pension or gratuity". (2): the President may
-- reduce or withhold where the person "has been convicted by any court of an offence (even if only a fine and no term of imprisonment
-- has been imposed) (a) under the Prevention of Corruption Act 1960; or (b) involving corruption under any other written law". (3): the
-- President "must, before exercising any power ... consider the record of the proceedings of the court".
GIVEN `convicted under the Prevention of Corruption Act 1960` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `convicted of another offence involving corruption` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `President has considered the court record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President may reduce or withhold the pension` IF
        (`convicted under the Prevention of Corruption Act 1960` OR `convicted of another offence involving corruption`)
    AND `President has considered the court record`
